    <string name="diag_code_permission_listener">Notification access is not granted. Tick AnyLyric in system settings, then come back.</string>
    <string name="diag_code_listener_unbound">Notification access is ticked, but the system has not bound the service yet. Tap Reconnect; if that fails, toggle the switch off and on in system settings.</string>
    <string name="diag_code_permission_overlay">Overlay permission is missing. Grant the display-over-other-apps permission.</string>
    <string name="diag_code_no_session">No app is publishing a media session. Start playback in the car player or a third-party player.</string>
    <string name="diag_code_session_inactive">A media session exists but is not playing. Press play in that app.</string>
    <string name="diag_code_avrcp_gate">The player updates the title only while paused. This is a publishing-side AVRCP limitation, not an AnyLyric bug.</string>
    <string name="diag_code_no_channel">This player exposes no lyric channel at all. Nothing is wrong with AnyLyric; another source would be needed.</string>
    <string name="diag_code_clock_unstable">The player reports a position that repeatedly jumps back a little. Timed lyrics may drift; the cause is on the publishing side.</string>
    <string name="diag_code_overlay_not_attached">The overlay was not attached. Check the overlay permission and try again.</string>
    <string name="diag_code_overlay_not_measured">The overlay is attached but has no size. Likely a layout problem.</string>
    <string name="diag_code_hidden_by_rule">Hidden on purpose by the visibility rule, for example when navigation is in front.</string>
    <string name="diag_code_ok">Working as designed. Lyrics are being taken from %1$s.</string>
